ExLlamaV3 (https://github.com/turboderp-org/exllamav3) is MIT-licensed.

This workstream keeps a pinned upstream commit
(`0c49587a7c235e6303a6bbedc8b665272ad3a2ea`) and applies an SM86 decode
overlay from `kernel/overlay/` at build time. The intended long-term home
for those kernel commits is the `phaelon74/exllamav3` fork, branch
`sm86-decode`, checked out as the `EXL3-vLLM/exllamav3` submodule.

The vLLM plugin talks to the resulting `exllamav3_ext` build. Keep the
conversion environment and the vLLM runtime environment separate.

Dense EXL3 vLLM glue is adapted from the dense subset of
https://github.com/local-inference-lab/vllm/pull/139 (Apache-2.0).
SparkInfer, routed MoE, GLM/DeepSeek, MLA/DCP, MTP, and rank-sliced expert
paths are intentionally not ported.
